-- ============================================
-- AGGREGATE FUNCTIONS
-- ============================================

-- Aggregate Functions:
-- Aggregate functions are used to perform calculations
-- on multiple rows and return a single result.

-- Main Aggregate Functions:
--
-- 1. COUNT()
--    Counts the number of rows/values.
--    Example: COUNT(salary)
--
-- 2. SUM()
--    Calculates the total of numeric values.
--    Example: SUM(salary)
--
-- 3. AVG()
--    Calculates the average of numeric values.
--    Example: AVG(salary)
--
-- 4. MAX()
--    Returns the highest value.
--    Example: MAX(salary)
--
-- 5. MIN()
--    Returns the lowest value.
--    Example: MIN(salary)
--
-- ============================================
-- IMPORTANT:
-- Aggregate Functions:
-- COUNT()  -> Number
-- SUM()    -> Total
-- AVG()    -> Average
-- MAX()    -> Highest
-- MIN()    -> Lowest
-- ============================================


